questions.question:
A + B means ‘A is the father of B’;

A × B means ‘A is the brother of B’;

A ÷ B means ‘A is the sister of B’.

Which of the following expressions means ‘H is the paternal grandson of P’?

questions.solution:
The pattern followed here is:

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2e1a2f0dc142ecfb544963c2209981c3e759d0cf81e91577dd86d50c0a2dc835.png] 

D + 1 → E; E + 1 → F; F + 1 → G; G + 1 → **H**;

J + 2 → L; L + 2 → N; N + 2 → P; P + 2 → **R**;

Q + 3 → T; T + 3 → W; W + 3 → Z; Z + 3 → **C**;

C + 4 → G; G + 4 → K; K + 4 → O; O + 4 → **S**

Hence, ‘HRCS’ is the correct answer.
